  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling the root causes of irregular migration and supporting integrated communities in Upper Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will cover 2 specific objectives:  SO1) To enhance 1,485 vulnerable young men and women&#x2019;s prospects of establishing a business or gaining employment in Assiut and Sohag. SO2) To promote positive alternatives and raise awareness of risks of irregular migration and ensure equal access to quality and child protection services for 2,655 families.     _x000d_
The project will work in 1 community in Assiut (Abnub district) and in 1 community in Sohag (Tahta district). The project beneficiaries will be as follows:_x000d_
- Direct beneficiaries: 4500 Female and Males aged from 15-30 years of which 60-65 % should be young women; _x000d_
- Indirect beneficiaries will be 22,500 people._x000d_
_x000d_
Final project outcomes will be added once the evaluation has been conducted and approved.</narrative>
  </description>
